+    decides the sample that would be used to test the order. MEASURED over every
+    archived routing pass (285 dispatched passes, reconstructed by replaying
+    `rank_falsifier_writers` against each run's own roster):
+
+        seat           on the ladder   actually asked
+        Codex-SIM                256              256
+        ChatGPT-SIM              216               54
+        DeepSeek-SIM             214                0
+        Gemini-SIM               203                0
+        CC2-SIM                  193              119
+        Fable-SIM                 84                0
+
+    3 of the 6 members were on the ladder a combined 501 times and asked ZERO
+    times, and 106 passes stopped short of the ladder's end without resolving. An
+    order with that exposure profile is not merely unmeasured, it is UNMEASURABLE
+    while in force. Rotating the starting point per experiment is what makes the
+    rung-1 stratum estimable at all.
+
+    A ROTATION, NOT A SHUFFLE, and the difference is measured rather than
+    preferred. Over k experiments a rotation puts each of the k members at rung 1
+    EXACTLY once; an independent uniform shuffle does so only in expectation, and
+    for k = 6 the probability that at least one member still has no rung-1
+    observation after 6 experiments is 1 - 6!/6^6 = 0.9845679. Exact coverage
+    dominates coverage-in-expectation on the named property "experiments needed
+    before every identity has a rung-1 observation", so the rotation is the
+    simpler mechanism AND the stronger one.
+
+    IT MAKES NO CAPABILITY CLAIM. A rotation of a set is not a ranking of it: the
+    caller still receives `established=False`, and the relative cycle of the input
+    is preserved exactly, so nothing about any seat's position is asserted to be
+    earned. `seed` of None returns the input UNCHANGED, so every existing caller
+    and every archived replay keeps the order it had.
+    """
+    seq = tuple(order)
+    text = str(seed or "").strip()
+    if not text or len(seq) < 2:
+        return seq
+    h = int(_hashlib.sha256(text.encode("utf-8")).hexdigest()[:16], 16)
+    k = h % len(seq)
+    return seq[k:] + seq[:k]
+
